UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"DSHX 0.2: plugin tooling for DeepSeek Harness 0.2, rebuilt end to end","description":"DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 moves the framework to DeepSeek Harness 0.2 with a protocol-2 adapter, Config-based settings, uiConversation events, peer-based RPC, and session format 4. This is a breaking release, and the migration guide covers every contract that changed.","sections":[{"id":"why-0-2-breaks","title":"Why 0.2 is a breaking release","paragraphs":["DeepSeek Harness 0.2 replaced the contracts DSHX 0.1 was built on. DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 does not keep the old generation behind an alias. It removes protocol-1, ships protocol-2, and asks every plugin to declare a 0.2 range in engines.dsh before it can build or run.","A compatibility layer was the tempting option, and we rejected it. Settings, conversation events, RPC admission, and session data all changed shape. Supporting both generations would have doubled the adapter surface and hidden the exact changes plugin authors need to make.","The cost is a migration for every existing plugin. The 0.1 to 0.2 guide walks through it with working code for each step, and create-dshx 0.2.0-preview.0 starts new projects on the new contracts."]},{"id":"what-we-verified","title":"What we verified, and what is still experimental","paragraphs":["The supported range is >=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0. The verified baseline is a source build of the dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2 tag, exercised by the real-runtime smoke suite for Host-only and Host/Client projects.","The npm artifact currently published as @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.1-rc.2 is not that build. It ships stale profile-boot code, so DSHX records it as experimental rather than verified. A version number tells you which package was installed; it does not tell you that the runtime booted. Until upstream republishes, use a source build for development and smoke testing.","The four status words are verified, compatible, experimental, and unsupported. They appear in dshx check, in diagnostics, and in the CLI capability output. The npm tags are independent: @becomeopc/dshx@preview points at 0.2.0-preview.0, while latest stays on 0.1.3."]},{"id":"settings","title":"Settings: one Config, no namespace","paragraphs":["In 0.1 a plugin declared a settings schema and registered it with a Host provider under a namespace it chose. In 0.2 the schema is the plugin Config, and DSH projects it into its own Settings form through SettingsForms. There is no namespace field, and nothing is registered at runtime.","defineSettings() still takes one Schemastery schema, so most definitions move unchanged. defineHost() now takes a single config contract instead of a settings array, and setup receives the config handle. DSHX marks the root schema volatile, so every field is live; marking an individual field volatile now throws.","Identity is the part that breaks quietly. DSH keys the form by the Host profile entry id that loads the plugin, not by a name the plugin picks. DSHX embeds that id in the Client artifact, so the plugin has to keep loading through the entry named in its bundle patch. Rename the entry, forget the patch, and the form still renders — it just reads and writes nothing.","On the Client, useSettings reads ctx.configForms.get(entryId). set and unset return booleans, and ordered edits use mutate with an expected revision. Secret fields report their schema position and whether a value is set. The value itself never leaves the Host."]},{"id":"conversation","title":"Conversation: uiConversation and session format 4","paragraphs":["Conversation contributions register through ctx.uiConversation.events.register. The conversationEvents service is gone, and renderer types now come from @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation/client. @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime is not part of DSH 0.2 at all: remove it from dependencies, peers, and dsh.client.inject.","defineConversation keeps its lifecycle shape, so most of the change is one call site and a few package edges. DSHX adds uiConversation to the Client inject list when a definition is present, and dshx check flags a missing package edge.","Session format 4 is where replay code tends to break. Only official SessionEventMap keys are accepted, sequence values are branded, and custom durable event types remain unsupported. There is no translation shim; rebuild persisted payloads against the official vocabulary."]},{"id":"connection","title":"Connection: peers, remote namespaces, and a launch token","paragraphs":["Host APIs register with connection.rpc.handle(channel, handler). The authority option is gone. The handler receives the official peer fact, and DSH decides admission. Client code no longer calls connection.api; generated Remote namespaces appear as ctx.remote.<namespace>, with $on and $stream for events.","DSHX keeps the author-facing shape of useApiQuery and the imperative bindings, and the wire path is unchanged from a plugin point of view: top-level /dshx-<hash>/<method> channels still carry the method in the DSHX envelope. The capability name changes to connection:peer-admission, so capability snapshots and checks need updating.","One operational change catches people by surprise. Browser requests now require the launch token that DSH hands to the page, exchanged at /connect?token=… for a signed session cookie before any /api call. Direct loopback requests without that cookie fail. Custom smoke runners and scripts need to perform the exchange; the DSHX Client runtime already does."]},{"id":"prompt-commands-tools","title":"Prompt, Commands, and Tools","paragraphs":["Prompt assembly uses personaPrefix and personaSuffix, and DSH allocates contribution order. definePromptSection and definePromptContext keep their order field, but it is a hint now, not a guarantee."],"items":["Command input exposes attachments instead of images, and a CommandResult may carry sourceEventSeq.","Tools no longer support the mode: both option. Native and PTC tools are declared separately.","ctx.codeRuntime becomes ctx.ptcRuntime, CallId becomes ToolCallId, and JsonValue comes from @deepseek-ai/dsh-util-values.","DSHX re-exports the official defineTool unchanged, so these names come from the official packages instead of DSHX wrappers."]},{"id":"fewer-wrappers","title":"Fewer wrappers, closer to DSH","paragraphs":["The result is fewer translation layers. Where 0.1 renamed or wrapped an upstream type, 0.2 passes the official one through. Editor hints and runtime errors line up with DSH documentation, and the names move when DSH moves — which is the point of a breaking release.","For plugin authors this is mostly a cleanup: fewer DSHX-specific names to learn, and fewer places where a type can drift from the package that owns it."]},{"id":"manifests-inspect","title":"Manifests, patches, and Inspect","items":["manifestVersion: 1 is accepted. engines.dsh is the preferred support declaration, with the @deepseek-ai/dsh peer dependency as the fallback. Keep a concrete devDependencies version for local builds.","dsh.bundle.patch may be a string or an array of paths. DSHX scans every patch to resolve the Settings entry id.","The /invariant subpath is gone. Import supported entries from the package root, /host, /client, /api, /settings, /experimental/conversation, or /tooling.","DSH 0.2 has no runtime Slot catalog. dshx inspect slots reports DSHX3204 because Slots are compile-time contracts. dshx add ui generates from explicit --slot and --provider values and emits DSHX6112, because the provider catalog cannot verify the registration.","Runtime Inspect for tools, services, events, and configs still works through the DSHX-owned Host bridge. It stays composition-scoped and does not depend on development-only DSH commits."]},{"id":"migrating","title":"How to migrate a plugin from 0.1 to 0.2","paragraphs":["The order below matches the migration guide. Each step is meant to be verifiable before moving to the next one."],"items":["Update metadata: move @becomeopc/dshx to 0.2.0-preview.0, pin @deepseek-ai/dsh to 0.2.1-rc.2 for local builds, add engines.dsh with >=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0, and remove @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime everywhere.","Move settings: keep the schema, drop the namespace, pass config to defineHost, read ctx.configForms on the Client, and rename capability checks to client:config-forms.","Update Conversation: replace ctx.conversationEvents.register with ctx.uiConversation.events.register, then rebuild against session format 4.","Update Connection: remove the authority option, switch Client calls to ctx.remote namespaces, and exchange the launch token at /connect for browser API access.","Update Prompt, Commands, and Tools: personaPrefix and personaSuffix, attachments, sourceEventSeq, ptcRuntime, ToolCallId, and the official JsonValue.","Validate: run dshx check, then pnpm smoke:dsh with --dsh-source pointing at a checkout of the tag. The smoke covers Settings writes and revision fences, Commands, Prompt contributions, Conversation replay, HMR, Host restart, and runtime Inspect."]},{"id":"availability","title":"What to expect from the preview","paragraphs":["DSHX and create-dshx are on npm’s preview channel as 0.2.0-preview.0. The stable latest channel stays on 0.1.3. create-dshx, the Phase A fixture, and the reference marketplace plugin already target the 0.2 line.","Use this release to migrate plugins and report contract gaps, not to run production deployments. The breaking changes are deliberate, the npm DSH artifact is still experimental, and the verified evidence comes from the source tag.","The next preview will tighten the migration based on what breaks in real projects. If something in the guide is wrong or missing, the issue tracker is the right place to say so."]}],"links":[{"label":"DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 on npm","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"create-dshx 0.2.0-preview.0 on npm","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/create-dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"0.1 to 0.2 migration guide","href":"https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility#migration"},{"label":"DeepSeek Harness compatibility and version status","href":"https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility"},{"label":"Browse DeepSeek Harness plugins on DSHX","href":"https://dshx.io/en/plugins"},{"label":"Release commit on GitHub","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/commit/eea4bdb475181f3f777d43672aa4f2b8268ead53"}]},"zh":{"title":"DSHX 0.2 发布：为 DeepSeek Harness 0.2 重建的插件工具链","description":"DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 跟进 DeepSeek Harness 0.2：protocol-2 适配器、基于 Config 的插件设置、uiConversation 会话事件、peer 路由 RPC 与 Session format 4。这是一次破坏性发布，迁移指南覆盖了每一个变化的契约。","sections":[{"id":"why-0-2-breaks","title":"为什么 0.2 是一次破坏性发布","paragraphs":["DeepSeek Harness 0.2 替换了 DSHX 0.1 赖以构建的契约。DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0 没有把旧一代藏在别名后面，而是移除 protocol-1、提供 protocol-2，并要求每个插件在 engines.dsh 中声明 0.2 范围后才能构建或运行。","兼容层是很容易想到的选项，我们没有采用。设置、会话事件、RPC 准入与会话数据都换了形状；同时支持两代会把适配器面积翻倍，还会掩盖插件作者真正需要处理的改动。","代价是每个已有插件都要迁移。0.1 到 0.2 指南为每一步提供了可运行的代码，create-dshx 0.2.0-preview.0 则让新项目直接落在新契约上。"]},{"id":"what-we-verified","title":"我们验证了什么，什么仍是实验性","paragraphs":["支持范围是 >=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0。验证基线是用 dsh-v0.2.1-rc.2 标签构建的源码，由真实运行时 smoke 覆盖 Host-only 与 Host/Client 项目。","npm 上以 @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.1-rc.2 发布的产物并不是这份构建。它包含过期的 profile 启动代码，因此 DSHX 把它记录为实验性，而不是已验证。版本号只能说明装了哪个包，不能说明运行时真的启动成功。在上游重新发布之前，请用源码构建做开发与 smoke 测试。","四个状态词分别是 verified、compatible、experimental、unsupported，会出现在 dshx check、诊断信息与 CLI 能力输出中。npm 标签是独立的：@becomeopc/dshx@preview 指向 0.2.0-preview.0，latest 仍停留在 0.1.3。"]},{"id":"settings","title":"Settings：一份 Config，没有命名空间","paragraphs":["在 0.1 里，插件声明设置 schema，再以自选命名空间注册到 Host provider。到了 0.2，这份 schema 就是插件 Config，DSH 通过 SettingsForms 把它投影成自己的设置表单。没有命名空间字段，运行时也不再注册任何东西。","defineSettings() 仍然接收一份 Schemastery schema，大多数定义可以原样迁移。defineHost() 改为接收单个 config 契约而不是 settings 数组，setup 会拿到 config 句柄。DSHX 会把根 schema 标记为 volatile，让所有字段实时生效；单独标记某个字段为 volatile 现在会抛错。","真正会静默出问题的是身份。DSH 用加载插件的 Host profile entry id 作为表单标识，而不是插件自选的名字。DSHX 把这个 id 写进 Client 产物，因此插件必须继续通过 bundle patch 中声明的 entry 加载。改了 entry、忘了 patch，表单仍然会渲染，只是读写都落不到任何地方。","在 Client 端，useSettings 读取 ctx.configForms.get(entryId)。set 与 unset 返回布尔值，有序修改使用带 expected revision 的 mutate。密钥字段只报告 schema 位置和是否已设置，值本身不会离开 Host。"]},{"id":"conversation","title":"Conversation：uiConversation 与 session format 4","paragraphs":["Conversation 贡献通过 ctx.uiConversation.events.register 注册。conversationEvents 服务已移除，渲染类型来自 @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation/client。@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime 已不属于 DSH 0.2，请从 dependencies、peers 与 dsh.client.inject 中删除。","defineConversation 的生命周期形状保持不变，所以大部分改动是一个调用点加上几处包边界。存在定义时，DSHX 会把 uiConversation 加入 Client 注入列表，dshx check 会报告缺失的包边界。","回放代码通常会在 session format 4 上出问题。只接受官方 SessionEventMap 的键，序列值带有品牌类型，自定义持久事件类型仍不受支持。这次没有翻译层，持久化的 payload 需要按官方词汇重建。"]},{"id":"connection","title":"连接：peer、remote 命名空间与启动令牌","paragraphs":["Host API 通过 connection.rpc.handle(channel, handler) 注册。authority 选项已移除，handler 会收到官方 peer 事实，由 DSH 决定是否准入。Client 不再调用 connection.api，生成的 Remote 命名空间以 ctx.remote.<namespace> 出现，事件使用 $on 与 $stream。","DSHX 保留了 useApiQuery 与命令式绑定的作者接口，插件视角下的线上路径也没有变化：顶层 /dshx-<hash>/<method> 通道仍在 DSHX envelope 中携带方法名。能力名称改为 connection:peer-admission，能力快照与检查需要同步更新。","有一处运营层面的变化容易让人措手不及。浏览器请求现在需要 DSH 交给页面的启动令牌，先访问 /connect?token=… 换取签名会话 cookie，之后才能调用 /api。没有该 cookie 的本地直连请求会失败。自定义 smoke runner 与脚本需要完成这次兑换，DSHX 自己的 Client 运行时已经内置。"]},{"id":"prompt-commands-tools","title":"Prompt、Commands 与 Tools","paragraphs":["Prompt 组装改用 personaPrefix 与 personaSuffix，贡献顺序由 DSH 统一分配。definePromptSection 与 definePromptContext 的 order 字段仍在，但它现在只是提示，不是保证。"],"items":["Command 输入使用 attachments 取代 images，CommandResult 可以携带 sourceEventSeq。","Tool 不再支持 mode: both 选项，native 与 PTC 工具需要分别声明。","ctx.codeRuntime 改为 ctx.ptcRuntime，CallId 改为 ToolCallId，JsonValue 来自 @deepseek-ai/dsh-util-values。","DSHX 原样重新导出官方 defineTool，这些名字直接来自官方包，而不是 DSHX 的包装层。"]},{"id":"fewer-wrappers","title":"更少的包装，更贴近 DSH","paragraphs":["结果是更少的翻译层。0.1 中由 DSHX 改名或包装的上游类型，在 0.2 中直接透传。编辑器提示与运行时错误因此和 DSH 文档一致，名称也会随 DSH 一起变化——这正是破坏性发布的意义。","对插件作者来说，这更像一次清理：需要记住的 DSHX 专有名称更少，类型也更难偏离拥有它的包。"]},{"id":"manifests-inspect","title":"清单、patch 与 Inspect","items":["接受 manifestVersion: 1。engines.dsh 是首选的支持声明，@deepseek-ai/dsh peer 依赖作为回退。本地构建仍应固定一个具体的 devDependencies 版本。","dsh.bundle.patch 可以是字符串，也可以是路径数组。DSHX 会扫描每个 patch 来解析 Settings entry id。","/invariant 子路径已移除。支持的入口从包根、/host、/client、/api、/settings、/experimental/conversation 或 /tooling 导入。","DSH 0.2 没有运行时 Slot 目录。由于 Slot 是编译期契约，dshx inspect slots 会返回 DSHX3204。dshx add ui 根据显式的 --slot 与 --provider 生成，并发出 DSHX6112，因为 provider 目录无法验证注册。","tools、services、events 与 configs 的运行时 Inspect 仍通过 DSHX 自有的 Host bridge 工作，保持 composition scope，不依赖仅存在于开发检出的 DSH 提交。"]},{"id":"migrating","title":"如何把插件从 0.1 迁移到 0.2","paragraphs":["下面的顺序与迁移指南一致，每一步都应该能单独验证，再进入下一步。"],"items":["更新元数据：把 @becomeopc/dshx 升到 0.2.0-preview.0，本地构建固定 @deepseek-ai/dsh 0.2.1-rc.2，加入 engines.dsh（>=0.2.1-rc.2 <0.3.0-0），并彻底移除 @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime。","迁移设置：保留 schema，去掉命名空间，把 config 传给 defineHost，在 Client 读取 ctx.configForms，并把能力检查改为 client:config-forms。","迁移 Conversation：用 ctx.uiConversation.events.register 替换 ctx.conversationEvents.register，再按 session format 4 重建。","迁移连接：移除 authority 选项，Client 改用 ctx.remote 命名空间，浏览器 API 先在 /connect 兑换启动令牌。","迁移 Prompt、Commands 与 Tools：personaPrefix 与 personaSuffix、attachments、sourceEventSeq、ptcRuntime、ToolCallId 以及官方 JsonValue。","验证：先跑 dshx check，再用 --dsh-source 指向标签检出的 pnpm smoke:dsh。smoke 覆盖设置写入与 revision 围栏、Commands、Prompt 贡献、Conversation 回放、HMR、Host 重启与运行时 Inspect。"]},{"id":"availability","title":"预览版说明","paragraphs":["DSHX 与 create-dshx 已以 0.2.0-preview.0 发布到 npm 的 preview 通道，稳定 latest 通道仍为 0.1.3。create-dshx、Phase A fixture 与参考 marketplace 插件都已面向 0.2 线。","这个版本适合迁移插件、报告契约缺口，不适合直接用于生产部署。破坏性变更是有意为之，npm 上的 DSH 产物仍属实验性，已验证的证据来自源码标签。","下一个预览版会根据真实项目中的破坏点收紧迁移流程。如果指南有错误或遗漏，请在 issue tracker 里指出。"]}],"links":[{"label":"npm 上的 DSHX 0.2.0-preview.0","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"npm 上的 create-dshx 0.2.0-preview.0","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/create-dshx/v/0.2.0-preview.0"},{"label":"0.1 到 0.2 迁移指南","href":"https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility#migration"},{"label":"DeepSeek Harness 兼容性与版本状态","href":"https://dshx.io/en/docs/compatibility"},{"label":"浏览 DSHX 上的 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/en/plugins"},{"label":"GitHub 发布提交","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/commit/eea4bdb475181f3f777d43672aa4f2b8268ead53"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'dshx-0-2-0-preview-0';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"Hub CLI 0.1.3: the operations prompt now lives in the Hub","description":"Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 removes the operations prompt from the public npm package. Agents fetch an administrator-only bundle instead, with encrypted resources and a pinned CLI version, so the prompt can change without a release.","sections":[{"id":"why-the-prompt-moved","title":"Why the prompt left the package","paragraphs":["The operations prompt is the most frequently edited file in the project. It describes how the agent researches, what it may write, how it reports, and what it must never expose. Every one of those rules gets refined as the catalog grows, and for a while each refinement meant a new CLI release.","That coupling was wrong. An operator could keep running an old prompt without noticing, and the public tarball carried administrator-facing instructions and resource-handling rules that had nothing to do with the CLI’s job.","0.1.3 moves the prompt and the bootstrap into the Hub. The npm package keeps the commands. The Hub keeps the instructions."]},{"id":"how-a-run-starts","title":"How a run starts now","paragraphs":["The bootstrap is short and stable. It tells the agent to run npx --yes --package @becomeopc/dshx-hub-cli@preview dshx-hub ops bundle --output <absolute private path>, then follow bundle.prompt exactly.","The bundle carries the full instructions, the exact command surface, the CLI version it was generated with, and the resources an administrator configured. The agent sets each resource key as an environment variable, never prints the values, and uses bundle.meta.cliVersion for every later dshx-hub command.","The version pin is what keeps a run reproducible. A stale, hand-edited, or locally reconstructed prompt is a failure, not a fallback."]},{"id":"administrator-changes","title":"What administrators control","items":["The bundle endpoint requires an administrator bearer token. A regular catalog token is not sufficient.","Administrators configure the allowlisted resources for a run, currently GITHUB_TOKEN, on the same page that previews the prompt.","Stored resource values are encrypted with AES-GCM in D1 using the AGENT_RESOURCE_KEY Worker secret. They are returned only inside an authenticated bundle.","The bundle command writes its output to a file with mode 0600 and never prints resource values.","The public CLI no longer bundles the prompt, and the old ops prompt command is gone."],"paragraphs":["The administrator page is also where the bootstrap comes from. It is generated from the current prompt, so an administrator never has to assemble it by hand."]},{"id":"version-convergence","title":"How version drift is handled","paragraphs":["The bootstrap stays on the stable preview channel, so it does not need to be re-copied when the CLI moves. If the installed CLI and the bundle disagree, the command returns agent_bundle_mismatch with error.details.expectedCliVersion.","The agent re-runs the same command with that exact version, at most twice. If it still fails, the run stops with the original error instead of continuing on an unverified CLI. A new prompt therefore reaches operators on the next run without anyone editing the bootstrap."]},{"id":"bundle-contents","title":"What the bundle contains","items":["bootstrap: the short text an administrator pastes into a new agent session.","prompt: the full operating instructions, including the mandatory start checklist, editorial policy, error handling, and reporting rules.","meta: the CLI version, the capabilities hash, the command surface, and the policy values the prompt refers to.","resources: the administrator-configured values, decrypted only for this authenticated response."],"paragraphs":["The CLI writes all of it to one file and never echoes the contents to the terminal, which keeps resource values out of shell history and logs."]},{"id":"why-no-fallback","title":"Why there is no local fallback","paragraphs":["A fallback prompt would defeat the point of moving the prompt into the Hub. If the bundle is unavailable, the agent cannot know whether the instructions it remembers are current, so it stops instead of guessing.","The same reasoning applies to CLI versions. The bundle records the version it was generated with, and every later command must use that exact version. Running a newer CLI against an older prompt, or the reverse, is treated as a mismatch rather than a best effort.","Administrators keep control of the release cadence. Updating the prompt changes the next run without an npm release, and the public package stays free of operational instructions."]},{"id":"operator-changes","title":"What changes for operators","items":["Remove any workflow that called ops prompt; the prompt now arrives through ops bundle.","Run ops preflight and ops begin as before, and keep the run ID, stopStartingAt, and leaseExpiresAt from the response.","Keep using per-write run IDs, checkpoints, and verification before ops finish.","The failure codes that matter to operators are unchanged: authentication_required, invalid_token, insufficient_scope, hub_edge_challenge, ops_run_active, ops_run_expired, revision_conflict, and idempotency_conflict."]},{"id":"what-stays","title":"What stays the same","paragraphs":["The catalog operations themselves do not change: source inspection, observation upserts, revisioned curation, visibility, submissions, media, audit, blog, featured shelves, and immutable reports.","The response envelope, partial-failure exit codes, idempotency rules, and report immutability are the same. A batch that returns HTTP 200 can still contain rejected items, and exit code 2 still means partial success."]},{"id":"how-to-judge","title":"How to judge whether it works","paragraphs":["The output of the prompt is public. The daily operations report at /operations shows what the agent researched, what it changed, and what it left open.","Read a few days rather than one. If the reports cite sources, separate confirmed writes from research, and state open items plainly, the bundle flow is doing its job. If they turn vague, the prompt is the first place to look.","The report is written by the same agent, so treat it as a claim with receipts, not as an audit. The Hub records the writes it accepted, and the report should match them."]},{"id":"availability","title":"Availability","paragraphs":["Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 is available on npm’s preview channel. The stable latest channel remains on 0.1.1.","The release notes are in the package changelog. The next step for an administrator is to review the prompt page and confirm the resource allowlist before the next scheduled run."]}],"links":[{"label":"Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 on npm","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx-hub-cli/v/0.1.3-preview.0"},{"label":"Hub CLI release notes","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/packages/framework-hub-cli/CHANGELOG.md"},{"label":"Read the public daily operations reports","href":"https://dshx.io/en/operations"},{"label":"DSHX Hub changelog","href":"https://dshx.io/en/changelog"}]},"zh":{"title":"Hub CLI 0.1.3：运营提示词搬进 Hub","description":"Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 把运营提示词从公开 npm 包中移除。Agent 改为获取管理员专属 bundle，其中包含加密资源与锁定的 CLI 版本，提示词的修改不再需要发版。","sections":[{"id":"why-the-prompt-moved","title":"为什么把提示词移出 npm 包","paragraphs":["运营提示词是这个项目里被修改最频繁的文件。它规定 Agent 如何调研、可以写什么、如何汇报，以及绝不能暴露什么。随着目录成长，这些规则每条都在细化，而此前每改一次都意味着发布一个新的 CLI 版本。","这种耦合是错的。运营端可能在毫无察觉的情况下继续运行旧提示词，公开 tarball 里也带着面向管理员的说明和资源处理规则，而它们与 CLI 的职责无关。","0.1.3 把提示词和引导语搬进 Hub。npm 包保留命令，Hub 保留说明。"]},{"id":"how-a-run-starts","title":"现在一轮运营如何开始","paragraphs":["引导语很短，也很稳定。它要求 Agent 运行 npx --yes --package @becomeopc/dshx-hub-cli@preview dshx-hub ops bundle --output <绝对且私密的路径>，然后严格按 bundle.prompt 执行。","bundle 包含完整说明、准确的命令面、生成它时使用的 CLI 版本，以及管理员配置的资源。Agent 把每个资源键设置为本轮环境变量，不打印这些值，并在之后所有 dshx-hub 命令中使用 bundle.meta.cliVersion。","版本锁定是运行可复现的关键。过期、手工修改或本地重建的提示词会被视为失败，而不是回退方案。"]},{"id":"administrator-changes","title":"管理员控制什么","items":["bundle 接口要求管理员 bearer token，普通 catalog token 不足以读取。","管理员在预览提示词的同一个页面配置本轮允许使用的资源，目前是 GITHUB_TOKEN。","保存的资源值在 D1 中使用 AES-GCM 加密，密钥是 Worker secret AGENT_RESOURCE_KEY；只有在通过认证的 bundle 中才会解密返回。","bundle 命令把内容写入权限为 0600 的文件，并且从不打印资源值。","公开 CLI 不再包含提示词文件，旧的 ops prompt 命令已移除。"],"paragraphs":["管理员页面也是引导语的来源。引导语由当前提示词生成，管理员不需要手工拼装。"]},{"id":"version-convergence","title":"版本漂移如何处理","paragraphs":["引导语固定在稳定的 preview 通道上，所以 CLI 前进时不需要重新复制它。如果本地安装的 CLI 与 bundle 不一致，命令会返回 agent_bundle_mismatch，并在 error.details.expectedCliVersion 中给出期望版本。","Agent 会用这个确切版本重跑同一条命令，最多两次。如果仍然失败，本轮会带着原始错误停止，而不是在未经验证的 CLI 上继续。因此新提示词会在下一轮自动到达运营端，不需要任何人修改引导语。"]},{"id":"bundle-contents","title":"bundle 里有什么","items":["bootstrap：管理员粘贴到新 Agent 会话里的短引导语。","prompt：完整操作说明，包括强制启动清单、编辑政策、错误处理与报告规则。","meta：CLI 版本、能力哈希、命令面，以及提示词引用的策略参数。","resources：管理员配置的值，只在这份通过认证的响应中解密。"],"paragraphs":["CLI 把全部内容写入一个文件，并且不会把内容回显到终端，从而避免资源值进入 shell 历史与日志。"]},{"id":"why-no-fallback","title":"为什么没有本地回退","paragraphs":["本地回退会抵消把提示词迁入 Hub 的意义。如果 bundle 不可用，Agent 无法确认自己记住的说明是否仍是最新版本，因此应当停止，而不是猜测。","CLI 版本也是同一个道理。bundle 记录了生成它时使用的版本，之后每条命令都必须使用这个确切版本。用更新的 CLI 搭配旧提示词，或反过来，都会被视为不匹配，而不是尽力而为。","发布节奏仍由管理员控制。修改提示词会改变下一轮运营，不需要发布 npm 版本，公开包也不再携带运营说明。"]},{"id":"operator-changes","title":"运营侧的变化","items":["移除任何调用 ops prompt 的流程；提示词现在通过 ops bundle 获取。","照常运行 ops preflight 与 ops begin，并保存响应中的 run ID、stopStartingAt 与 leaseExpiresAt。","继续在每次写入时携带 run ID，使用 checkpoint，并在 ops finish 前完成验证。","运营关心的错误码没有变化：authentication_required、invalid_token、insufficient_scope、hub_edge_challenge、ops_run_active、ops_run_expired、revision_conflict 与 idempotency_conflict。"]},{"id":"what-stays","title":"哪些部分保持不变","paragraphs":["目录操作本身没有变化：来源检查、observation upsert、带 revision 的内容编辑、可见性、投稿、媒体、审计、博客、精选榜单，以及不可变的运营报告。","响应 envelope、部分失败退出码、幂等规则与报告不可变性都保持不变。HTTP 200 的批量响应仍可能包含被拒绝的条目，退出码 2 仍然表示部分成功。"]},{"id":"how-to-judge","title":"如何判断它是否在工作","paragraphs":["提示词的产出是公开的。/operations 上的每日运营报告会展示 Agent 研究了什么、改了什么、留下了什么。","与其只看一天，不如连着读几天。如果报告引用来源、区分调研与已确认写入、并直接列出未完成事项，说明 bundle 流程在正常工作；如果内容变得含糊，先检查提示词。","报告由同一个 Agent 撰写，因此应当把它看作带凭证的主张，而不是审计本身。Hub 记录了实际接受的写入，报告应与之一致。"]},{"id":"availability","title":"获取方式","paragraphs":["Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0 已发布到 npm 的 preview 通道，稳定 latest 通道仍为 0.1.1。","发布说明在包的 changelog 里。管理员下一步应审阅提示词页面，并在下一次计划运行前确认资源白名单。"]}],"links":[{"label":"npm 上的 Hub CLI 0.1.3-preview.0","href":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@becomeopc/dshx-hub-cli/v/0.1.3-preview.0"},{"label":"Hub CLI 发布记录","href":"https://github.com/liyown/dshx/blob/main/packages/framework-hub-cli/CHANGELOG.md"},{"label":"阅读公开的每日运营报告","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/operations"},{"label":"DSHX Hub 更新日志","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/changelog"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'hub-cli-0-1-3-preview-0';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"The DSHX Hub journal, and ten shelves for DeepSeek Harness plugins","description":"DSHX Hub now publishes bilingual editorial articles and ten featured shelves covering 52 DeepSeek Harness plugins. The point is not another ranking: it is to say what a recommendation can and cannot claim.","sections":[{"id":"fifty-two","title":"Fifty-two plugins and no way to choose","paragraphs":["A catalog can tell you that 52 DeepSeek Harness plugins exist. It cannot tell you which three are worth an afternoon. Search answers existence, stars measure attention, and a flat category list puts a skin, a memory layer, and a remote-control bridge in the same row.","The featured page is our attempt at the missing layer. It arranges 52 plugins into ten shelves by the job they do, in an order an editor is willing to defend.","It is deliberately not a ranking. There is no score, no vote count, and no paid placement. A shelf is a short list with a point of view."]},{"id":"ten-shelves","title":"Ten shelves, organized by job","paragraphs":["The shelves are Skins and Interface, Remote and Mobile, Memory and Context, Models and Access, Agents and Automation, Developer Workbench, Browser and Multimodal, Markets and Trust, Session and Rewind, and Fun and Experiments.","Each shelf is an ordered list, and an empty shelf is cleared rather than left with stale picks. Every pick links to its plugin page, so a reader can move from a recommendation to the install target in one step. The page is bilingual, and so is every shelf name."]},{"id":"what-a-pick-means","title":"What a pick does not mean","paragraphs":["A pick is not a security review, a compatibility guarantee, or a promise that the plugin survives the next DSH release. It means an editor looked at the source, the README, and the install target, and judged the plugin worth trying for that job.","Featured is also separate from the quality flag the catalog computes, and separate from search ranking. A plugin can be excellent and still absent from a shelf, because the shelf is full or the job is already covered.","We wrote the first journal article to make that boundary explicit. It is easier to state the limits now than to walk them back later."]},{"id":"journal","title":"The journal","paragraphs":["Articles are longer than a changelog entry and shorter than documentation. They explain how a plugin was evaluated, how a category is changing, or how to get a tool running when the README assumes too much.","The launch pieces are the curation article and a full install guide for dsh-whale-widget, a free DSH Web balance widget. The guide covers the install commands, the bubble setup, and the fixes for the problems people actually hit.","Future posts follow the same rule: one specific subject, evidence you can check, and a clear statement of what the article leaves out."]},{"id":"choosing","title":"How picks are chosen, and retired","paragraphs":["Picks come from source evidence: the README, repository activity, the declared install target, publisher facts, and the public Hub entry. Only published plugins appear; hidden entries drop out even if they were picked earlier.","Shelves are re-checked when a plugin changes version, when a repository goes quiet, or when a better option appears for the same job. Removing a pick is not a verdict on the author. Usually the plugin moved, the install target changed, or the category found a better answer.","Article links follow the same rule. A link to a plugin that is later hidden gets corrected instead of left to rot."]},{"id":"for-authors","title":"For plugin authors","items":["Publish a stable identity and one unambiguous, structurally safe install target.","Write a README that covers what the plugin does, how to configure it, and its limitations. The Hub keeps the original README and records its content hash.","Provide bilingual names, short descriptions, and overviews that stand on their own. Placeholder copy and generic keyword lists are rejected.","Choose accurate categories and tags. A plugin that is honest about its scope is easier to place on a shelf.","Keep the entry current. A stale version, a dead repository, or a broken install target is a reason to remove a pick."]},{"id":"using-both","title":"How to use the two surfaces","paragraphs":["The shelves are for choosing. They answer a narrow question: for this job, which plugins are worth a look, and in what order. The journal is for understanding: why a plugin is on a shelf, what it costs to run, and where it stops being a good fit.","Search and category pages remain the complete index. The editorial surfaces sit on top of the catalog rather than replacing it, so a plugin that is not featured is still discoverable."]},{"id":"start-here","title":"Where to start","paragraphs":["Start with the curation article to see how the shelves are framed, or browse the featured page by category. If you maintain a plugin, the plugin pages and the submission path explain what a complete entry looks like."]}],"links":[{"label":"Read the DSHX Hub journal","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog"},{"label":"Browse featured DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/featured"},{"label":"Curating 52 DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog/curating-52-deepseek-harness-plugins"},{"label":"dsh-whale-widget: DSH balance widget install guide","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog/dsh-whale-widget-guide"},{"label":"Browse all DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/plugins"},{"label":"DSHX Hub changelog","href":"https://dshx.io/en/changelog"}]},"zh":{"title":"DSHX Hub 博客上线，并新增十个 DeepSeek Harness 插件榜单","description":"DSHX Hub 新增双语编辑博客，以及覆盖 52 个 DeepSeek Harness 插件的十个精选榜单。重点不是再做一个排行榜，而是说清推荐能主张什么、不能主张什么。","sections":[{"id":"fifty-two","title":"52 个插件，却没有办法选","paragraphs":["目录可以告诉你存在 52 个 DeepSeek Harness 插件，却无法告诉你哪三个值得花一个下午。搜索回答的是存在性，star 数衡量的是关注度，而扁平分类列表会把皮肤、记忆层和远程控制桥接放进同一行。","精选页是对这层缺失的补充。它按任务把 52 个插件整理成十个榜单，并给出编辑愿意为之负责的顺序。","它刻意不是排行榜：没有评分，没有票数，也没有付费位置。榜单就是一份有观点的短名单。"]},{"id":"ten-shelves","title":"按任务划分的十个榜单","paragraphs":["十个榜单分别是皮肤与界面、远程与移动、记忆与上下文、模型与接入、Agent 与自动化、开发者工作台、浏览器与多模态、市场与信任、会话与回溯、趣味与实验。","每个榜单都是有序列表，没有有效推荐的榜单会被清空，而不是保留过期条目。每个推荐都链接到插件页面，读者可以从推荐一步走到安装目标。页面与榜单名称都提供中英文。"]},{"id":"what-a-pick-means","title":"推荐不代表什么","paragraphs":["推荐不是安全审查，不是兼容性保证，也不承诺插件在下一个 DSH 版本之后仍然可用。它只表示编辑看过源码、README 与安装目标，并判断这个插件值得为该任务一试。","精选也与目录计算的质量标记是两回事，与搜索排序无关。一个插件可能很优秀却不在榜单上，因为榜单已经满了，或这个任务已有更合适的答案。","首批文章把这条边界写清楚了。现在说明限制，比以后往回找补要容易。"]},{"id":"journal","title":"博客","paragraphs":["文章比更新日志长，比文档短。它们解释一个插件如何被评估、某个分类正在发生什么变化，或者当 README 假设太多时，如何把工具真正跑起来。","首批文章是榜单整理记录，以及 dsh-whale-widget 的完整安装指南。后者是一个免费的 DSH Web 余额挂件，指南覆盖安装命令、气泡设置，以及用户实际会遇到的修复方法。","之后的文章遵循同一规则：一个具体主题，可核对的证据，并明确说明文章没有覆盖什么。"]},{"id":"choosing","title":"推荐如何选出，又如何退役","paragraphs":["推荐来自来源证据：README、仓库活跃度、声明的安装目标、发布者信息，以及插件在 Hub 上的公开条目。只有已发布插件会出现；被隐藏的条目即使曾经入选也会退出。","插件版本变化、仓库长期没有动静，或同一任务出现更好的选择时，榜单会重新检查。移除推荐并不代表对作者的评价，通常只是插件迁移了、安装目标变了，或这个分类有了更好的答案。","文章链接遵循同一规则。如果文章指向的插件后来被隐藏，链接会被修正，而不是留在那里失效。"]},{"id":"for-authors","title":"插件作者如何进入候选","items":["提供稳定的身份，以及一个明确、结构安全的安装目标。","README 要说明插件做什么、如何配置，以及有哪些限制。Hub 保留原始 README，并记录其内容哈希。","提供能独立成立的双语名称、简短描述与概览。占位文案和泛化关键词列表会被拒绝。","选择准确的分类与标签。对自己的适用范围诚实的插件，更容易被放进合适的榜单。","保持条目更新。版本过期、仓库失效或安装目标损坏，都是移除推荐的理由。"]},{"id":"using-both","title":"如何配合使用博客与榜单","paragraphs":["榜单用来做选择，回答一个很窄的问题：为这个任务，哪些插件值得看，应该按什么顺序看。博客用来理解原因：某个插件为什么在榜单上、运行成本如何，以及在什么情况下不再合适。","搜索与分类页面仍然是完整索引。编辑入口叠加在目录之上，而不是取代目录，因此没有被推荐的插件依然可以被找到。"]},{"id":"start-here","title":"从哪里开始","paragraphs":["可以先读榜单的整理文章，了解这些推荐如何被界定，或按分类浏览精选页。如果你在维护插件，插件页面与投稿入口会说明一个完整条目应该包含什么。"]}],"links":[{"label":"阅读 DSHX Hub 博客","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/blog"},{"label":"浏览精选 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/featured"},{"label":"52 个 DeepSeek Harness 插件的整理记录","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog/curating-52-deepseek-harness-plugins"},{"label":"dsh-whale-widget 余额挂件安装指南","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog/dsh-whale-widget-guide"},{"label":"浏览全部 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/plugins"},{"label":"DSHX Hub 更新日志","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/changelog"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'hub-editorial-blog-and-featured-shelves';
--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE changelog_entries SET content_json = '{"en":{"title":"A public daily log of how the DSHX plugin catalog is maintained","description":"Every day the catalog is maintained, DSHX Hub publishes an operations report: what the agent researched, what it changed, what it could not verify, and what is still open. Reports are Markdown, immutable, and merged into one page per day.","sections":[{"id":"agent","title":"The catalog changes without anyone at the keyboard","paragraphs":["The DSHX Hub catalog is maintained by an autonomous operations agent. It searches the ecosystem, inspects sources, admits plugins, edits copy, and fixes metadata. Most days it changes something; some days it decides that nothing is worth changing.","A catalog that edits itself needs receipts. The operations report records what the agent looked at, what it changed, what it could not verify, and what it deliberately skipped. Without it, readers can only see the result and guess at the reasoning.","The reports are public for the same reason the plugin pages are. History makes an entry easier to trust, and plugin authors can see why a description, a category, or an install target changed."]},{"id":"one-page-per-day","title":"One page per day","paragraphs":["The agent can run several times a day. Each run used to publish its own report, which turned the history into a pile of short notes and made the list hard to follow.","Reports now group by the Asia/Shanghai calendar day. The newest report is the page body. When it is cumulative and starts with the daily merge marker, earlier runs for that day are hidden. Without the marker, earlier runs stay available in a collapsed section, so work published before the merge rule existed is not lost.","The page shows the day’s run count, first start, latest completion, and combined outcome. Up to 20 earlier runs are listed, with a count of any beyond that. The cap keeps a busy day readable without dropping the summary."]},{"id":"contents","title":"What a report contains","paragraphs":["Reports are GitHub-Flavored Markdown with stable headings, so a reader can skim the first screen and know whether the day changed anything."],"items":["Work completed: confirmed writes, with the plugin and the action.","Evidence and verification: the sources checked and the results that supported a claim.","Open items: material work left incomplete, blockers, and what would resolve them.","Research notes: the queries and candidates inspected, including honest zero-result days."]},{"id":"reading","title":"Reading a report without over-trusting it","paragraphs":["The most useful distinction in a report is between research, attempted writes, confirmed writes, and skipped work. A plugin named as a candidate was not necessarily admitted. A write described as attempted was not necessarily confirmed.","A zero-write day can be honest. The prompt requires a minimum research effort before declaring that nothing was worth changing, and it requires the queries and rejection reasons to be recorded. A report that claims work without a receipt is a bug, not a summary.","Reports end as completed or partial. Partial means material work was left unfinished. It is more useful than rounding up, and it is not a failure of the catalog."]},{"id":"markdown","title":"Why Markdown","paragraphs":["Markdown is the format the agent already writes. It handles tables and lists, and it diffs cleanly when the prompt or the report template changes.","The Hub renders reports through a restricted pipeline: no raw HTML, no images, no tracking pixels. The daily merge marker is an HTML comment, so it is stripped from the visible page and never appears to readers.","Both locales follow the same rules. English and Chinese bodies must carry the same facts and conclusions, not a thin translation of each other."]},{"id":"related-plugins","title":"The plugin list on each page","paragraphs":["Each day page lists the plugins the run touched, with the actions recorded in the audit ledger. The association uses the report actor and a server-clock window based on the run lease, because the CLI keeps checkpoints locally and the Hub only learns the run ID when the report is published.","The list is a navigation aid, not a complete changelog. A plugin can change outside the audit window, and the report body remains the authoritative account."]},{"id":"omitted","title":"What is deliberately missing","items":["Credentials, token prefixes, and authentication headers.","Email addresses, private URLs, and local file paths.","Raw stack traces and internal audit payloads.","Raw HTML, images, and tracking pixels."],"paragraphs":["These exclusions are part of the reporting contract, not an afterthought. A report is meant to be publishable as-is, so anything that would need redaction before publication is disallowed at write time."]},{"id":"why","title":"Why publish the process","paragraphs":["Most catalogs publish outcomes and keep the process private. Doing the opposite costs something: mistakes are visible, and so are slow days.","What it buys is a catalog that can be audited. If a description looks wrong, the report shows which source was read. If a plugin disappears, the report says why. That is a firmer basis for trust than a badge.","It also makes the agent easier to improve. A vague report, a skipped verification, or a claim without a receipt is a visible failure, and the next prompt revision can target it."]},{"id":"follow","title":"Where to follow","paragraphs":["The operations log lives at /operations and is grouped by day. Each day has a stable URL such as /operations/2026-10-21; older run-based URLs redirect to the day page with a 301.","The changelog covers product changes to the Hub and the framework. The journal covers the plugin ecosystem. Together they show what changed, why, and what it cost."]}],"links":[{"label":"Read the daily operations reports","href":"https://dshx.io/en/operations"},{"label":"Operations report for 2026-10-21","href":"https://dshx.io/en/operations/2026-10-21"},{"label":"DSHX Hub changelog","href":"https://dshx.io/en/changelog"},{"label":"Read the DSHX Hub journal","href":"https://dshx.io/en/blog"},{"label":"Browse DeepSeek Harness plugins","href":"https://dshx.io/en/plugins"}]},"zh":{"title":"DSHX 插件目录的公开运营日报","description":"目录维护的每一天，DSHX Hub 都会发布运营报告：Agent 研究过什么、改了什么、哪些无法验证、还留下什么未完成事项。报告使用 Markdown，不可修改，并按天合并成一个页面。","sections":[{"id":"agent","title":"目录在没有人值守时发生变化","paragraphs":["DSHX Hub 的插件目录由自动化运营 Agent 维护。它会搜索生态、检查来源、收录插件、修改文案、修复元数据。大多数日子它会改动一些东西，也有些日子它判断没有值得改的内容。","一个会自己编辑的目录需要凭证。运营报告记录 Agent 看过什么、改了什么、哪些无法验证，以及哪些工作被有意跳过。没有这份记录，读者只能看到结果，再去猜原因。","报告公开的理由和插件页面一样：历史让条目更容易被信任，插件作者也能看到某段描述、某个分类或某个安装目标为什么变了。"]},{"id":"one-page-per-day","title":"一天一个页面","paragraphs":["Agent 一天可能运行多次。过去每次运行都单独发布报告，历史被切成一堆短记录，列表也很难读。","现在报告按 Asia/Shanghai 日历日归组，当天最新的一份作为页面正文。如果它是累计报告并以每日合并标记开头，同一天较早的运行会被隐藏；没有标记时，较早的运行保留在折叠区域，因此合并规则生效之前发布的工作不会丢失。","页面显示当天的运行次数、最早开始时间、最新完成时间与合并结果。最多列出 20 次较早运行，并说明还有多少未展示。这个上限让繁忙的一天保持可读，同时不丢掉摘要。"]},{"id":"contents","title":"报告里有什么","paragraphs":["报告使用 GitHub-Flavored Markdown，并采用稳定标题，读者扫一眼首屏就能知道这一天有没有产生变化。"],"items":["Work completed：已确认的写入，以及对应的插件与操作。","Evidence and verification：检查过的来源，以及支持结论的结果。","Open items：未完成的重要工作、阻塞项，以及解决它们需要什么。","Research notes：执行过的查询与检查过的候选，也包括诚实的零结果日。"]},{"id":"reading","title":"读报告时不要过度信任","paragraphs":["报告最有用的地方，是区分调研、尝试写入、确认写入与跳过的工作。被列为候选的插件不一定被收录；被描述为尝试的写入不一定成功。","零写入的一天也可以是诚实的。提示词要求在宣布无事可做之前完成最低限度的调研，并要求记录查询与拒绝理由。没有凭证却声称做了工作，是缺陷，不是总结。","报告以 completed 或 partial 结束。partial 表示有重要工作尚未完成，它比四舍五入成 completed 更有用，也不是目录的失败。"]},{"id":"markdown","title":"为什么用 Markdown","paragraphs":["Markdown 本来就是 Agent 写作的格式。它支持表格与列表，在提示词或报告模板变化时也容易对比差异。","Hub 使用受限的渲染管线：不允许原始 HTML、图片与追踪像素。每日合并标记是一个 HTML 注释，会从可见页面中移除，读者永远看不到它。","中英文遵循同一规则。两种语言的正文必须承载相同的事实与结论，而不是互相的简略翻译。"]},{"id":"related-plugins","title":"页面上的相关插件","paragraphs":["每个日报页面列出本轮涉及的插件，以及审计账本中记录的操作。关联依据是报告的执行者与基于运行租约的服务端时间窗，因为 CLI 在本地保存 checkpoint，Hub 只有在报告发布时才得知 run ID。","这份列表是导航辅助，不是完整的变更日志。插件的变化可能发生在审计时间窗之外，报告正文仍然是权威记录。"]},{"id":"omitted","title":"刻意省略的内容","items":["凭据、token 前缀与认证头。","邮箱地址、私有 URL 与本地文件路径。","原始堆栈与内部审计 payload。","原始 HTML、图片与追踪像素。"],"paragraphs":["这些排除项是报告契约的一部分，而不是事后补救。报告要能原样发布，因此任何需要在发布前打码的内容，在写入时就不允许出现。"]},{"id":"why","title":"为什么公开过程","paragraphs":["多数目录只发布结果，把过程留在内部。反过来做是有代价的：错误可见，低产出的日子也可见。","换来的是一个可审计的目录。如果某段描述看起来不对，报告会显示读过哪个来源；如果某个插件消失，报告会说明原因。这比一个徽章更适合作为信任基础。","它也让 Agent 更容易改进。含糊的报告、跳过的验证、没有凭证的主张都是可见的失败，下一次提示词修订可以针对这些问题。"]},{"id":"follow","title":"在哪里持续关注","paragraphs":["运营日志位于 /operations，按天分组。每天都有稳定 URL，例如 /operations/2026-10-21；旧的基于 run ID 的 URL 会以 301 跳转到日报页面。","更新日志记录 Hub 与框架的产品变化，博客记录插件生态。三者合起来，可以看到改了什么、为什么改，以及付出了什么代价。"]}],"links":[{"label":"阅读每日运营报告","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/operations"},{"label":"2026-10-21 运营报告","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/operations/2026-10-21"},{"label":"DSHX Hub 更新日志","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/changelog"},{"label":"阅读 DSHX Hub 博客","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/blog"},{"label":"浏览 DeepSeek Harness 插件","href":"https://dshx.io/zh/plugins"}]}}', revision = revision + 1, updated_at = strftime('%s','now') * 1000 WHERE slug = 'hub-daily-operations-reports';
